    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0325" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg277"/>

                <head>No. 144.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Pierrepont.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 1,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, London:</hi></p>
                <p>Thornton, by note, proposes resumption extradition under treaty, <pb facs="0326"
                        n="278" xml:id="pg278"/> without demanding stipulations, as in Winslow’s
                    ease. Have replied expressing satisfaction with decision to remove obstacle to
                    extradition, with hope that Winslow, Brent, and Gray will now be surrendered,
                    and stating, on receiving indication of readiness so to do, agent will be
                    authorized to receive them, and thereafter we will be ready to grant
                    requisitions.</p>
                <p>Copy correspondence sent by mail. Make, no advances. Watch question. If notified
                    of any step to surrender fugitives, advise me promptly.</p>
                <closer><signed>FISH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
